'''telephone''' (tel′ẹ̄-fōn), ''n.'' [= F. ''téléphone'' = G. ''telephon'' = Sw. Dan. ''telefon'' (all after E.); < Gr. τῆλε, afar, + φωνή, voice, sound.] An instrument or apparatus for the transmission of sound to a distant point. {{smaller|The word is generally restricted to devices for the transmission of articulate speech by the agency of electricity. The process consists essentially of the transmission of electric waves or impulses which agree in period and phase with atmospheric waves produced by sound. These in turn, by means of an electromagnet,}}
